How to interact with database? 

Ans:- Spring makes database interaction under much easier compared to plain jdbc.
--> To interact with database in spring boot, it provides a very powerful concept called spring data jpa.
--> this model is build on top of jpa (JAVA PERSISTANCE API ) and makes database operations extremely easy by removing the need for most boilerplate code.
--> with Spring DATA JPA , you can perform CRUD(CREATE, READ, UPDATE , DELETE) Operations , pagination, Sorting, and even complex Query- often without writing a single line of SQL.

** JPA, Hibernate and SPRING JPA:- 
1. JPA:- type : - specifictions (not an implementations)
         purpose:- Defines a set of interfae=ce and annotations for ORM(Object realtion mapping) operations.
2. Hibernate:- type:- ORM framework(implementation of jpa + it own native API)
         Prupose:- implements JPA-> makes JPA Interface Work.
             --> provides it OWN native API (more powerful and features- rich than standard JPA.
3. SPRING BOOT And JPA:- 
--> In SPRING BOOT JPA is used as Specifications.
--> By Default, spring BOOT  uses hibernate  + JPA implemetations
--> without extra   , using JPA + hibernate means
      . manual repository creation
       . manual method writing
       . manual wiring
4. Spring DATA JPA:- 
-- > type: - part of the spring data family.
--> purpose:- simplifies jpa usage in spring boot by removing boiler plate code.
--> working on TOp of : JPA--> Hibernate.

    key features:-
       . automatically creates repository implements at runtime.
       . no need to write sql for most CRUD OPerations.
       . supports methods- name based on Queries.

Main Interface:- 
    CRUD Interface
    JPA interface
Note:- In spring boot , when we create an interface like myRepo and extends JPA Repository , we don't write any code for methods such as findBy() --> we only declare that we want them.
--> when the application starts , spring automatically creates a special objects for our interfaces that already has the working code inside.


Q. Difference b/w CRUD Repository and JPA Repository ?
Ans:- 
1. CRUD Repository :- 
--> Basic database operations : Save() , findById(), etc
--> Good for simple CRUD WORK.
less features.

2. JPA Repository:-
--> includes everything from CRUD Repository 
--> ADD extra JPA-related feautres like 
     1. pagination.
     2. sorting
     3. Batch operation
in short:- 
. JPA Repository =  CRUD Repository + Extra features for pagination, sorting and advacned JPA support.

                           Repository 
                               ↑
                               ↑
                          CRUD Operation
                               ↑
                               ↑
                          Pagination and sorting
                               ↑
                               ↑
                            JPA Repository

**** Spring DATA JPA automatically implements repository methods if you follow a specific naming convention
--> methods like findByName(), containing are called derived methods, and springboot automatically genreate their implements at runtime , so you don't have to write custom Queries manually.

**** common keywords in spring DATA JPA methods names
--> these keywords are used after your entity fieldname in methods name, spring data JPA wil create these QUery automatically
    keywords                             Examplemethods
--> findby                                findByName
--> GREATER than                           findByGraterThan

